+## Optional: CompliR counterparty screening
+
+The Compliance Engine check runs in the browser before the send dialog submits. Setting `COMPLIR_URL` to a [CompliR](https://github.com/mrnetwork0001/complir) host adds a second, server-side check in `/api/payout` and `/api/wallet/transfer`: the recipient's risk tier is read from `GET /api/v1/attestation/<address>` (free; tiers are mirrored to the CompliR registry on [Arc mainnet](https://explorer.arc.network/address/0xA82EDb5e111c31C63E06EF0007f2fa1a9e7EB30d)). `HIGH` returns `403` with a `userMessage`; `LOW`/`MEDIUM` proceed. The two checks are independent and the stricter one wins; a CompliR timeout or outage fails open with a warning so it never blocks on its own downtime. The paid `POST /api/v1/screen` (x402, 0.01 USDC on Arc) returns a fresh verdict with reasons and recommended limits and is the upgrade path.
 
